</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Pretrain Experiments</h2>

<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Pretraining Details</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We adopt DeiT-Tiny <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">Touvron et al., 2021</a>)</cite> as the backbone for VER-T, DeiT-Small  <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">Touvron et al., 2021</a>)</cite> for VER-S, and ViT-Base <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dosovitskiy et al., 2020</a>)</cite> for VER-B. We choose the last <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=3</annotation></semantics></math> layers as Vision Expert Library (VEL). The projection head <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{i}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{i}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> consists of shallow CNNs, following the same design of Theia <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shang et al., 2024</a>)</cite>. The training dataset is ImageNet-1K <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Deng et al., 2009</a>)</cite>. We initialize the model weights using Theia and train VER on four A6000 GPUs for 50 epochs. The learning schedule consists of a linear warmup for the first 10% of training steps, followed by a constant learning rate of 0.002 for the next 40%, and then Cosine Annealing LR for the remaining steps.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Mutual Information Loss</h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In order to calculate <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{mi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{mi}</annotation></semantics></math>, we need to get <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\mathcal{I}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\mathcal{I}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\mathcal{E}_{l}^{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>l</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\mathcal{E}_{l}^{n})</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A3.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\mathcal{I}_{i},\mathcal{E}^{n}_{l})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>l</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\mathcal{I}_{i},\mathcal{E}^{n}_{l})</annotation></semantics></math>. <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\mathcal{E}^{n}_{l})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>l</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\mathcal{E}^{n}_{l})</annotation></semantics></math> can be calculated by counting the number of selection times of expert <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math> across all teacher vision foundation models. We assume each teacher model is equally important so <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\mathcal{I}_{i})=\frac{1}{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>I</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\mathcal{I}_{i})=\frac{1}{I}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of teacher models. For <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\mathcal{I}_{i},\mathcal{E}^{n}_{l})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>l</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\mathcal{I}_{i},\mathcal{E}^{n}_{l})</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A3.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\mathcal{I}_{i},\mathcal{E}^{n}_{l})=p(\mathcal{I}_{i})p(\mathcal{E}^{n}_{l}|\mathcal{I}_{i})=\frac{1}{I}p(\mathcal{E}^{n}_{l}|\mathcal{I}_{i})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>l</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>l</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>I</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>l</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\mathcal{I}_{i},\mathcal{E}^{n}_{l})=p(\mathcal{I}_{i})p(\mathcal{E}^{n}_{l}|\mathcal{I}_{i})=\frac{1}{I}p(\mathcal{E}^{n}_{l}|\mathcal{I}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><math id="A3.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\mathcal{E}^{n}_{l}|\mathcal{I}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>l</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\mathcal{E}^{n}_{l}|\mathcal{I}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> can be calculated by counting the number of selection times of expert <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>th teacher model.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3 </span>Pretraining Results</h3>

<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A3.T7" title="Table 7 ‣ C.3 Pretraining Results ‣ Appendix C Pretrain Experiments ‣ VER: Vision Expert Transformer for Robot Learning via FoundationDistillation and Dynamic Routing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> demonstrates the distillation performance compared with Theia. We can see that our VER can achieve better distillation performance with similar active parameters. And VER-S with less active and total parameters achieve comparable distillation performance compared to Theia-B.</p>
</div>
